      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has these understandability issues:\n- Massive unused import list (30+ unused static ChronoField imports and many unused type imports)\n- Unused class-level constants (`YEAR_STANDARD`, `YEAR_LEAP`, `STANDARD_YEAR_LENGTH`, `LEAP_YEAR_LENGTH`, `PARIS`)\n- `assertEquals(null, ...)` calls where `assertNull(...)` is clearer\n- No grouping comments to distinguish supported vs unsupported query results\n\nI'll write the improved version now.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes 30+ unused imports and 5 unused constants, replaces `assertEquals(null, ...)` with `assertNull(...)` for clarity, and adds a brief comment grouping supported vs. unsupported query results — all without changing runtime behaviour."
